$ jailops jail create web --image freebsd-15 --network lan --storage default
jail/web created

$ jailops jail create db --image freebsd-15 --network lan --storage default --label audit=critical
jail/db created

$ jailops jail audit web
CHECK                  RESULT   DETAIL
root.links             PASS     no link out of the root on a path the base's packages own
accounts.uid0          PASS     root and toor are the only accounts with uid 0
pkg.base_repository    PASS     FreeBSD-base is disabled inside the jail; the host upgrades the base
pkg.kmods_repository   PASS     FreeBSD-ports-kmods is disabled inside the jail
pkg.vulnerabilities    PASS     pkg audit names no vulnerable package

jail/web: 0 critical, 0 warning(s)

$ jailops jail audit web --suggest
CHECK                  RESULT   DETAIL
root.links             PASS     no link out of the root on a path the base's packages own
accounts.uid0          PASS     root and toor are the only accounts with uid 0
pkg.base_repository    PASS     FreeBSD-base is disabled inside the jail; the host upgrades the base
pkg.kmods_repository   PASS     FreeBSD-ports-kmods is disabled inside the jail
pkg.vulnerabilities    PASS     pkg audit names no vulnerable package
cron.jitter            PASS     suggestion: cron starts the jobs of root (periodic among them) at a random second: cron_flags="-J 60"
disk.limit             INFO     suggestion: the jail has no disk limit: it can fill its storage

Fix:
  disk.limit (suggestion): jailops config set web resources.disk=10G (a size that fits the jail)

jail/web: 0 critical, 0 warning(s)

$ jailops jail audit db
CHECK                  RESULT     DETAIL
root.links             PASS       no link out of the root on a path the base's packages own
accounts.uid0          CRITICAL   accounts with uid 0 besides root and toor: backdoor
pkg.base_repository    PASS       FreeBSD-base is disabled inside the jail; the host upgrades the base
pkg.kmods_repository   PASS       FreeBSD-ports-kmods is disabled inside the jail
pkg.vulnerabilities    PASS       pkg audit names no vulnerable package

Fix:
  accounts.uid0: remove each account (jailops exec db -- pw userdel NAME) unless you made it on purpose, and find out how it got there

jail/db: 1 critical, 0 warning(s)
[exit 1]

$ jailops jail audit db -o json
{
  "jail": "db",
  "running": false,
  "critical": 1,
  "warnings": 0,
